Hold on.

257
00:37:15.075 --> 00:37:16.188
Are you injured?

258
00:37:17.476 --> 00:37:18.588
Are you shot?

259
00:37:24.388 --> 00:37:25.849
Do exactly what I say!

260
00:37:25.891 --> 00:37:27.746
Exactly!

261
00:37:27.780 --> 00:37:31.325
Don't move unless I say.
Don't make a sound unless I say.

262
00:37:31.363 --> 00:37:32.475
Do you understand?

263
00:37:33.540 --> 00:37:35.452
- Do you understand?
- Yes! Yes!

264
00:37:35.494 --> 00:37:37.282
Please, don't hurt me.

265
00:37:54.467 --> 00:37:56.224
I'm here to help you.

266
00:37:56.260 --> 00:37:59.489
I'm Reese, Sergeant Techcom,
BN38416...

267
00:37:59.524 --> 00:38:00.865
assigned to protect you.

268
00:38:00.900 --> 00:38:02.525
You've been targeted
for termination.

269
00:38:07.844 --> 00:38:12.155
Attempt to intercept, 1-L19.

270
00:38:12.199 --> 00:38:13.954
This is 1-L19.

271
00:38:13.989 --> 00:38:16.095
Westbound on Olympic
approaching Overland.

272
00:38:20.549 --> 00:38:22.915
This is a mistake.

273
00:38:22.950 --> 00:38:24.355
I didn't do anything.

274
00:38:24.388 --> 00:38:26.014
No, but you will.

275
00:38:26.052 --> 00:38:28.157
It's very important
that you live.

276
00:38:28.196 --> 00:38:29.756
This isn't true.

277
00:38:29.797 --> 00:38:31.487
How could that man
just get up after you...

278
00:38:31.524 --> 00:38:34.371
He's not a man... a machine.

279
00:38:34.404 --> 00:38:37.819
A Terminator.
A Cyberdyne Systems Model 101.

280
00:38:45.635 --> 00:38:47.874
A machine?

281
00:38:47.911 --> 00:38:49.503
Like a robot?

282
00:38:49.542 --> 00:38:52.804
Not a robot. A cyborg.

283
00:38:52.838 --> 00:38:53.982
A cybernetic organism.

284
00:38:54.022 --> 00:38:56.836
- No. He was bleeding.
- Just a second.

285
00:38:59.687 --> 00:39:01.092
Get your head down!

286
00:39:44.130 --> 00:39:45.560
All right, listen.

287
00:39:45.603 --> 00:39:47.577
The Terminator's
an infiltration unit...

288
00:39:47.618 --> 00:39:48.928
part man, part machine.

289
00:39:48.962 --> 00:39:51.450
Underneath, it's a hyperalloy
combat chassis...

290
00:39:51.490 --> 00:39:55.516
microprocessor controlled,
fully armored... very tough.

291
00:39:55.555 --> 00:39:58.175
But outside,
it's living human tissue...

292
00:39:58.213 --> 00:40:02.522
flesh, skin, hair, blood...
grown for the cyborgs.

293
00:40:02.565 --> 00:40:04.387
- Look, I don't know what...
- Pay attention!

294
00:40:04.421 --> 00:40:06.331
I got to ditch this car.

295
00:40:11.748 --> 00:40:14.115
The 600 series had rubber skin.

296
00:40:14.148 --> 00:40:16.995
We spotted them easy,
but these are new.

297
00:40:17.028 --> 00:40:18.434
They look human...

298
00:40:18.467 --> 00:40:20.703
sweat, bad breath, everything.

299
00:40:20.740 --> 00:40:22.049
Very hard to spot.

300
00:40:22.083 --> 00:40:24.505
I had to wait till he moved
on you before I could zero him.

301
00:40:25.635 --> 00:40:27.260
Look...

302
00:40:27.300 --> 00:40:29.121
I am not stupid, you know.

303
00:40:29.154 --> 00:40:31.129
They cannot make things
like that yet.

304
00:40:31.170 --> 00:40:33.442
Not yet.

305
00:40:33.477 --> 00:40:35.069
Not for about forty years.

306
00:40:37.509 --> 00:40:39.549
Are you saying
it's from the future?

307
00:40:39.589 --> 00:40:42.523
One possible future.

308
00:40:42.565 --> 00:40:45.053
From your point of view...
I don't know tech stuff.

309
00:40:46.628 --> 00:40:49.049
Then you're from the future,
too, is that right?

310
00:40:49.092 --> 00:40:51.196
- Right.
- Right.

311
00:40:58.819 --> 00:41:01.023
Cyborgs don't feel pain.

312
00:41:01.059 --> 00:41:04.441
I do. Don't do that again.

313
00:41:04.482 --> 00:41:08.163
- Just let me go.
- Listen and understand!

314
00:41:08.197 --> 00:41:10.531
That Terminator is out there.

315
00:41:12.005 --> 00:41:13.663
It can't be bargained with.

316
00:41:13.700 --> 00:41:15.424
It can't be reasoned with.

317
00:41:15.461 --> 00:41:20.131
It doesn't feel
pity or remorse or fear.

318
00:41:20.166 --> 00:41:24.507
And it absolutely
will not stop ever!

319
00:41:24.549 --> 00:41:25.956
Until you are dead.

320
00:41:35.556 --> 00:41:36.985
Can you stop it?

321
00:41:41.252 --> 00:41:42.680
I don't know.

322
00:41:44.419 --> 00:41:46.786
With these weapons,
I don't know.

323
00:42:02.690 --> 00:42:05.341
All units. Gray Ford suspect
vehicle has been found...

324
00:42:05.378 --> 00:42:07.681
in a parking structure
at Fourth and Beaudry.

325
00:42:50.787 --> 00:42:52.444
Why me?

326
00:42:54.722 --> 00:42:56.187
Why does it want me?

327
00:43:02.628 --> 00:43:04.188
There was a nuclear war...

328
00:43:06.404 --> 00:43:08.030
a few years from now.

329
00:43:10.691 --> 00:43:13.080
All this...

330
00:43:13.123 --> 00:43:15.065
this whole place, everything...

331
00:43:16.260 --> 00:43:17.535
it's gone.

332
00:43:19.395 --> 00:43:20.769
Just gone.

333
00:43:21.730 --> 00:43:23.453
There were survivors.

334
00:43:23.490 --> 00:43:25.792
Here, there.

335
00:43:28.035 --> 00:43:29.627
Nobody even knew who started it.

336
00:43:33.156 --> 00:43:35.938
It was the machines, Sarah.

337
00:43:35.973 --> 00:43:37.762
I don't understand.

338
00:43:37.796 --> 00:43:39.836
Defense network computers...

339
00:43:41.027 --> 00:43:43.995
New... powerful

340
00:43:45.317 --> 00:43:46.877
Hooked into everything.

341
00:43:46.916 --> 00:43:48.443
Trusted to run it all.

342
00:43:49.828 --> 00:43:52.064
They say it got smart...

343
00:43:52.100 --> 00:43:55.580
a new order of intelligence.

344
00:43:55.620 --> 00:43:57.082
Then it saw all people
as a threat...

345
00:43:57.124 --> 00:43:59.011
not just the ones
on the other side.

346
00:44:00.868 --> 00:44:03.071
Decided our fate
in a microsecond...

347
00:44:04.578 --> 00:44:06.466
extermination.

348
00:44:20.545 --> 00:44:21.973
Did you see this war?

349
00:44:35.617 --> 00:44:38.616
I grew up after it
in the ruins...

350
00:44:38.656 --> 00:44:41.692
starving, hiding from HKs.

351
00:44:41.731 --> 00:44:43.586
- HKs?
- Hunter-Killers...

352
00:44:44.642 --> 00:44:47.457
patrol machines
built in automated factories.

353
00:44:48.514 --> 00:44:50.074
Most of us were rounded up...

354
00:44:50.114 --> 00:44:52.535
put in camps
for orderly disposal.

355
00:44:54.306 --> 00:44:56.859
This was burned in
by laser scanner.

356
00:45:00.578 --> 00:45:02.814
Some of us were kept alive...

357
00:45:02.849 --> 00:45:05.468
to work...

358
00:45:05.505 --> 00:45:07.195
loading bodies.

359
00:45:08.385 --> 00:45:10.840
The disposal units
ran night and day.

360
00:45:10.881 --> 00:45:13.880
We were that close
to going out forever.

361
00:45:16.928 --> 00:45:19.778
But there was one man
who taught us to fight...

362
00:45:19.811 --> 00:45:22.298
to storm the wire
of the camps...

363
00:45:22.338 --> 00:45:26.648
to smash those
metal motherfuckers into junk.

364
00:45:26.690 --> 00:45:28.665
He turned it around.

365
00:45:28.706 --> 00:45:30.113
He brought us back
from the brink.

366
00:45:30.145 --> 00:45:32.763
His name is Connor...

367
00:45:32.802 --> 00:45:34.395
John Connor.

368
00:45:34.433 --> 00:45:35.807
Your son, Sarah.

369
00:45:37.025 --> 00:45:38.617
Your unborn son.

370
00:47:23.937 --> 00:47:25.343
Drive!

371
00:47:54.881 --> 00:47:56.953
- They'll kill you.
- You in the Cadillac!

372
00:47:56.993 --> 00:47:58.302
Let me see your hands now!

373
00:48:01.185 --> 00:48:02.297
Get out of the car!

374
00:48:05.856 --> 00:48:08.093
Drop to your knees!

375
00:48:08.128 --> 00:48:09.470
Out of the car.

376
00:48:09.504 --> 00:48:10.933
Drop to the ground.

377
00:48:40.514 --> 00:48:42.423
Sarah,
try to drink some of this.

378
00:48:45.569 --> 00:48:47.576
Listen, are you sure it's them?

379
00:48:47.616 --> 00:48:50.583
Maybe I should look
at the bodies.

380
00:48:50.625 --> 00:48:52.697
No. They've been identified.
There's no doubt.

381
00:48:52.737 --> 00:48:54.525
Oh, God.

382
00:49:03.775 --> 00:49:05.717
Sarah, this is Dr. Silberman.

383
00:49:05.759 --> 00:49:06.904
Hi, Sarah.

384
00:49:06.944 --> 00:49:09.561
I want you to tell him
everything Reese told you.

385
00:49:09.599 --> 00:49:10.908
Do you feel up to that?

386
00:49:10.942 --> 00:49:12.949
I guess so.

387
00:49:14.495 --> 00:49:16.056
You're a doctor?

388
00:49:16.095 --> 00:49:18.550
Criminal psychologist.

389
00:49:18.591 --> 00:49:19.867
Is Reese crazy?

390
00:49:19.903 --> 00:49:23.326
That's what
we're gonna find out.

391
00:50:44.224 --> 00:50:47.769
So, you're a soldier,
fighting for whom?

392
00:50:48.864 --> 00:50:51.767
With the 132nd, under Perry.

393
00:50:51.808 --> 00:50:54.393
From 21 to 27.

394
00:50:54.432 --> 00:50:57.181
That's the year 2027?

395
00:50:57.216 --> 00:50:59.125
That's right.
And I was assigned...

396
00:50:59.168 --> 00:51:00.543
This is fucking great.

397
00:51:00.576 --> 00:51:02.911
...the last two years
under John Connor.

398
00:51:02.944 --> 00:51:04.154
Who was the enemy again?

399
00:51:04.191 --> 00:51:06.973
A computer defense system
built for...

400
00:51:07.008 --> 00:51:08.502
Damn. Sorry.

401
00:51:08.543 --> 00:51:11.859
Built for SAC-NORAD
by Cyberdyne Systems.

402
00:51:11.903 --> 00:51:13.310
I see.

403
00:51:13.343 --> 00:51:16.823
And this computer
thinks it can win...

404
00:51:16.862 --> 00:51:19.709
by killing
the mother of its enemy.

405
00:51:19.742 --> 00:51:22.840
Killing him, in effect,
before he's even conceived...

406
00:51:22.878 --> 00:51:25.114
a sort of retroactive abortion?

407
00:51:26.269 --> 00:51:28.310
That guy Silberman
cracks me up.

408
00:51:28.350 --> 00:51:29.975
Last week, he had this guy
in here that burned his Afghan.

409
00:51:30.013 --> 00:51:31.737
Screwed it first,
then he set it on fire.

410
00:51:31.773 --> 00:51:32.788
Shut up.

411
00:51:32.829 --> 00:51:34.901
Why didn't the computer
just kill Connor then?

412
00:51:34.941 --> 00:51:37.364
Why this elaborate scheme
with the Terminator?

413
00:51:37.406 --> 00:51:38.900
It had no choice.

414
00:51:38.941 --> 00:51:41.691
Their defense grid was smashed.

415
00:51:41.725 --> 00:51:43.154
We'd won.

416
00:51:43.197 --> 00:51:45.947
Taking out Connor then
would make no difference.

417
00:51:45.981 --> 00:51:48.886
Skynet had to wipe out
his entire existence.

418
00:51:48.928 --> 00:51:51.033
Is that when you
captured the lab complex...

419
00:51:51.071 --> 00:51:52.763
and found that...
What is it called?

420
00:51:52.800 --> 00:51:55.996
The time displacement equipment?

421
00:51:56.031 --> 00:52:00.188
That's right. The Terminator
had already gone through.

422
00:52:00.223 --> 00:52:03.038
Connor sent me to intercept,
and they blew the whole place.

423
00:52:03.071 --> 00:52:04.959
How are you supposed get back?

424
00:52:04.991 --> 00:52:06.779
I can't.

425
00:52:08.511 --> 00:52:10.136
Nobody goes home.

426
00:52:12.062 --> 00:52:14.680
Nobody else comes through.

427
00:52:14.717 --> 00:52:18.553
It's just him... and me.

428
00:53:58.406 --> 00:54:01.124
It's just him... and me.

429
00:54:03.429 --> 00:54:06.277
Why didn't you bring
any weapons...

430
00:54:06.309 --> 00:54:09.091
something more advanced?

431
00:54:09.126 --> 00:54:11.681
Don't you have ray guns?

432
00:54:11.720 --> 00:54:13.214
Ray guns.

433
00:54:13.257 --> 00:54:15.525
Show me a piece
of future technology.

434
00:54:15.560 --> 00:54:17.348
You go naked.

435
00:54:17.384 --> 00:54:19.554
Something about the field
generated by a living organism.

436
00:54:19.591 --> 00:54:22.079
- Nothing dead will go.
- Why?

437
00:54:22.120 --> 00:54:24.224
I didn't build
the fucking thing!

438
00:54:24.263 --> 00:54:28.573
OK. But this cyborg,
if it's metal...

439
00:54:28.615 --> 00:54:29.825
Surrounded by living tissue!

440
00:54:29.862 --> 00:54:31.172
Right.

441
00:54:31.207 --> 00:54:32.418
This is great stuff.

442
00:54:32.455 --> 00:54:34.342
I could make a career
out of this guy.

443
00:54:34.375 --> 00:54:35.968
You see how clever
this part is?

444
00:54:36.007 --> 00:54:37.665
How it doesn't require
a shred of proof?

445
00:54:37.702 --> 00:54:39.393
Most paranoid delusions
are intricate...

446
00:54:39.430 --> 00:54:41.285
but this is brilliant.

447
00:54:41.318 --> 00:54:44.000
Why were the other
two women killed?

448
00:54:44.038 --> 00:54:46.692
Most of the records
were lost in the war.

449
00:54:46.728 --> 00:54:49.150
Skynet knew almost nothing
about Connor's mother.

450
00:54:49.193 --> 00:54:52.935
Her full name, where she lived.
They just knew the city.

451
00:54:52.969 --> 00:54:55.302
The Terminator was
just being systematic.

452
00:54:55.335 --> 00:54:56.863
Well, let's go back to...

453
00:54:56.904 --> 00:54:59.871
Look, you have heard enough!
I have answered your questions!

454
00:54:59.911 --> 00:55:01.886
Now I have to see Sarah Connor!

455
00:55:01.928 --> 00:55:03.870
I'm afraid that's not up to me.

456
00:55:03.911 --> 00:55:05.437
Then why am I talking to you?

457
00:55:05.479 --> 00:55:07.071
Because I can help you.

458
00:55:07.111 --> 00:55:09.020
Who is in authority here?
Shut up!

459
00:55:09.063 --> 00:55:12.478
You still don't get it, do you?

460
00:55:12.519 --> 00:55:14.209
He'll find her.

461
00:55:14.246 --> 00:55:16.035
That's what he does!

462
00:55:16.071 --> 00:55:17.696
That's all he does!

463
00:55:17.734 --> 00:55:19.589
You can't stop him!

464
00:55:19.621 --> 00:55:21.378
He'll wade through you,
reach down her throat...

465
00:55:21.414 --> 00:55:23.205
and pull her fucking heart out!

466
00:55:23.240 --> 00:55:24.419
Doc.

467
00:55:24.457 --> 00:55:25.734
Let go of me...

468
00:55:28.456 --> 00:55:30.343
Sorry.

469
00:55:35.336 --> 00:55:36.995
So, Reese is crazy?

470
00:55:37.033 --> 00:55:40.382
In technical terminology...
he's a loon.

471
00:55:40.425 --> 00:55:44.614
Sarah, this is what
they call body armor.

472
00:55:44.648 --> 00:55:46.502
Our TAC guys wear these.

473
00:55:46.536 --> 00:55:48.608
It'll stop a 12-gauge round.

474
00:55:48.647 --> 00:55:51.014
This other individual must have
worn one under his coat.

475
00:55:51.047 --> 00:55:52.705
Feel that. Go ahead.

476
00:55:54.471 --> 00:55:56.293
What about when he punched
through the windshield?

477
00:55:56.327 --> 00:55:58.182
He was probably on PCP.

478
00:55:58.214 --> 00:56:01.149
Broke every bone in his hand
and wouldn't feel it for hours.

479
00:56:01.191 --> 00:56:02.881
There was this guy once...
See this scar?

480
00:56:02.918 --> 00:56:05.023
- Here.
- Thank you.

481
00:56:05.062 --> 00:56:06.752
There's a couch
in this other room.

482
00:56:06.790 --> 00:56:09.211
Why don't you stretch out
and try to get some sleep?

483
00:56:09.253 --> 00:56:11.905
It'll be an hour before your
mother gets here from Big Bear.

484
00:56:11.942 --> 00:56:14.811
- I can't sleep.
- Try.

485
00:56:14.853 --> 00:56:18.748
It may not look it, but
that couch is very comfortable.

486
00:56:19.781 --> 00:56:22.302
You'll be perfectly safe.

487
00:56:22.342 --> 00:56:25.091
We got 30 cops in this building.

488
00:56:25.126 --> 00:56:26.555
Thank you.

489
00:56:32.676 --> 00:56:34.108
Good night.

490
00:56:48.487 --> 00:56:50.341
I'm a friend of Sarah Connor.

491
00:56:50.374 --> 00:56:52.578
I was told that she's here.
Could I see her, please?

492
00:56:52.614 --> 00:56:54.621
No. You can't see her.
She's making a statement.

493
00:56:54.662 --> 00:56:55.709
Where is she?

494
00:56:55.750 --> 00:56:57.637
Look, it may take a while.

495
00:56:57.670 --> 00:56:59.775
If you want to wait,
there's a bench over there.

496
00:57:10.215 --> 00:57:12.070
I'll be back.

497
00:57:37.381 --> 00:57:40.251
What the hell was that?

498
00:57:48.264 --> 00:57:49.408
Gunshot!

499
00:57:58.280 --> 00:57:59.840
What is it, terrorists?

500
00:57:59.880 --> 00:58:01.287
Let's go! Let's go!

501
00:58:05.063 --> 00:58:06.656
Stay here.

502
00:58:19.718 --> 00:58:22.980
Let's get out of here!
Come on!

503
00:58:23.015 --> 00:58:24.607
He's got an automatic weapon!

504
00:58:26.022 --> 00:58:27.931
Move it, move it!

505
00:58:38.500 --> 00:58:40.256
What the hell
happened to the lights?

506
00:58:44.900 --> 00:58:46.329
Watch him.

507
00:59:05.926 --> 00:59:07.136
Automatic weapons!

508
00:59:07.175 --> 00:59:08.636
Lock and load! Let's go!

509
00:59:35.110 --> 00:59:36.604
Fire! Fire!

510
01:00:27.974 --> 01:00:29.381
This way.

511
01:01:08.292 --> 01:01:10.179
KFLB Newstime 4:36.

512
01:01:10.212 --> 01:01:12.416
In the top story of the hour...

513
01:01:12.452 --> 01:01:15.005
the largest single
law enforcement mobilization...

514
01:01:15.044 --> 01:01:17.378
in California history
is currently underway.

515
01:01:17.412 --> 01:01:18.941
Police in
five southern counties...

516
01:01:18.983 --> 01:01:20.990
are engaged in a massive manhunt
for an unident...

517
01:01:24.135 --> 01:01:25.563
Take this.

518
01:01:28.326 --> 01:01:30.846
All right,
let's get this off the road.

519
01:02:00.806 --> 01:02:03.970
- You cold?
- Freezing.

520
01:02:19.588 --> 01:02:21.213
You got a first name?

521
01:02:21.252 --> 01:02:23.391
Kyle.

522
01:02:23.428 --> 01:02:25.370
Kyle...

523
01:02:25.412 --> 01:02:27.932
what's it like
when you go through time?

524
01:02:30.342 --> 01:02:31.771
White light.

525
01:02:34.663 --> 01:02:36.092
Pain.

526
01:02:38.502 --> 01:02:40.389
It's like being born maybe.

527
01:02:40.421 --> 01:02:43.140
Oh, my God.

528
01:02:43.174 --> 01:02:45.924
I caught one back there.

529
01:02:45.958 --> 01:02:48.707
You mean you got shot?

530
01:02:48.741 --> 01:02:49.952
It's not bad.

531
01:02:49.989 --> 01:02:52.324
We got to get you to a doctor.

532
01:02:52.358 --> 01:02:54.246
It's OK. Forget it.

533
01:02:54.278 --> 01:02:57.126
What do you mean, forget it?
Are you crazy?

534
01:02:57.158 --> 01:02:59.198
Take this off.

535
01:03:10.500 --> 01:03:12.289
Jesus.

536
01:03:12.324 --> 01:03:14.877
See, it passed
right through the meat.

537
01:03:14.916 --> 01:03:17.087
This is going to make me puke.

538
01:03:17.123 --> 01:03:19.295
Would you talk about something?

539
01:03:19.332 --> 01:03:20.641
What?

540
01:03:20.676 --> 01:03:22.911
I don't know.
Anything. Just talk.

541
01:03:22.947 --> 01:03:24.986
Tell me about my son.

542
01:03:25.028 --> 01:03:27.874
He's about my height.

543
01:03:30.275 --> 01:03:33.145
He has your eyes.

544
01:03:35.875 --> 01:03:37.915
What's he like?

545
01:03:37.955 --> 01:03:40.322
You trust him.

546
01:03:40.358 --> 01:03:42.627
He's got a strength.

547
01:03:42.662 --> 01:03:45.345
I'd die for John Connor.

548
01:03:47.492 --> 01:03:51.454
Well... at least now
I know what to name him.

549
01:03:51.493 --> 01:03:54.274
I don't suppose
you know who the father is...

550
01:03:54.308 --> 01:03:57.058
so I won't tell him
to get lost when I meet him.

551
01:03:57.092 --> 01:03:59.459
John never said much about him.

552
01:03:59.492 --> 01:04:01.380
I know he dies before the war...

553
01:04:01.412 --> 01:04:02.841
Wait!

554
01:04:04.292 --> 01:04:06.299
I don't want to know.

555
01:04:06.339 --> 01:04:10.016
So, was it John
that sent you here?

556
01:04:10.052 --> 01:04:11.480
I volunteered.

557
01:04:12.450 --> 01:04:14.044
Why?

558
01:04:14.083 --> 01:04:17.697
It was a chance
to meet the legend...

559
01:04:17.734 --> 01:04:19.589
Sarah Connor.

560
01:04:19.621 --> 01:04:24.607
Taught her son to fight,
organize...

561
01:04:24.645 --> 01:04:26.816
prepare from when he was a kid.

562
01:04:26.853 --> 01:04:29.242
When you were in hiding
before the war...

563
01:04:32.133 --> 01:04:34.621
You're talking about things
I haven't done yet...

564
01:04:34.661 --> 01:04:36.003
in the past tense.

565
01:04:36.037 --> 01:04:38.240
It's driving me crazy.

566
01:04:41.732 --> 01:04:44.514
Are you sure
you have the right person?

567
01:04:44.547 --> 01:04:45.954
I'm sure.

568
01:04:45.988 --> 01:04:47.395
Come on.

569
01:04:47.427 --> 01:04:50.110
Do I look like
the mother of the future?

570
01:04:51.751 --> 01:04:54.118
Am I tough, organized?

571
01:04:54.150 --> 01:04:56.538
I can't even
balance my checkbook.

572
01:04:59.237 --> 01:05:02.139
Look, Reese,
I didn't ask for this honor...

573
01:05:02.181 --> 01:05:04.702
and I don't want it!
Any of it!

574
01:05:07.942 --> 01:05:10.397
Your son gave me a message
to give to you.

575
01:05:10.438 --> 01:05:11.998
Made me memorize it.

576
01:05:12.037 --> 01:05:15.965
Thank you, Sarah, for your
courage through the dark years.

577
01:05:16.005 --> 01:05:18.012
I can't help you with
what you must soon face...

578
01:05:18.052 --> 01:05:20.540
except to say that
the future is not set.

579
01:05:20.581 --> 01:05:23.101
You must be stronger
than you imagine you can be.

580
01:05:23.140 --> 01:05:26.751
You must survive,
or I will never exist.

581
01:05:26.788 --> 01:05:28.511
That's all.

582
01:05:30.628 --> 01:05:32.515
That's a good field dressing.

583
01:05:33.988 --> 01:05:35.875
You like it?

584
01:05:35.908 --> 01:05:38.111
It's my first.

585
01:05:41.283 --> 01:05:43.999
Get some sleep.
It will be light soon.

586
01:05:59.362 --> 01:06:01.272
Talk to me some more.

587
01:06:04.165 --> 01:06:06.531
About what?

588
01:06:06.564 --> 01:06:08.953
Tell me about where you're from.

589
01:06:11.364 --> 01:06:12.793
All right.

590
01:06:14.244 --> 01:06:16.666
You stay down by day...

591
01:06:16.708 --> 01:06:19.075
but at night
you can move around.

592
01:06:19.108 --> 01:06:22.588
You still have to be careful
because the HKs use infrared.

593
01:06:24.323 --> 01:06:27.138
But they're not too bright.

594
01:06:27.172 --> 01:06:30.519
John taught us ways
to dust them.

595
01:06:30.563 --> 01:06:33.823
That's when the infiltrators
started to appear.

596
01:06:33.858 --> 01:06:35.516
The Terminators
were the newest...

597
01:06:35.555 --> 01:06:36.929
the worst.

598
01:06:46.373 --> 01:06:48.576
Traversing your sector
in search mode.

599
01:06:48.611 --> 01:06:51.578
750 meters north
of your position.

600
01:06:51.621 --> 01:06:53.889
Understand. 750 meters north.

601
01:06:55.459 --> 01:06:56.986
Let's go.

602
01:06:57.028 --> 01:06:58.783
Intercept. Over.

603
01:06:58.819 --> 01:07:01.405
Take it easy.
Finish your sweep.

604
01:07:01.443 --> 01:07:03.581
They are scavenger teams
in that quadrant.

605
01:07:03.619 --> 01:07:05.025
Avoid contact.

606
01:07:05.059 --> 01:07:06.881
Repeat, avoid contact.

607
01:07:06.915 --> 01:07:08.376
We'll get them later.

608
01:07:08.418 --> 01:07:10.328
Roger, Echo Leader.

609
01:07:16.134 --> 01:07:17.759
Sector niner,
what's your status?

610
01:07:17.797 --> 01:07:19.455
Situation normal.

611
01:07:24.517 --> 01:07:25.661
We're coming in.

612
01:07:25.701 --> 01:07:27.610
Roger.

613
01:07:32.901 --> 01:07:37.636
Firebase,
what's your status? Over.

614
01:07:40.036 --> 01:07:42.208
Reese. BN384.

615
01:07:42.244 --> 01:07:43.673
Right. Let him in.

616
01:07:47.716 --> 01:07:50.563
Any infiltrators
at the shopping mall?

617
01:07:50.595 --> 01:07:53.443
No problem.
They were clean.

618
01:07:53.475 --> 01:07:56.323
We're cutting short
the patrol. Over.

619
01:07:56.355 --> 01:07:59.704
Roger, Yankee-1-7.
You are clear to return.

620
01:09:11.619 --> 01:09:13.725
Terminator!

621
01:10:27.488 --> 01:10:29.660
I was dreaming about dogs.

622
01:10:31.105 --> 01:10:34.105
We use them
to spot Terminators.

623
01:10:34.145 --> 01:10:36.699
Your world is pretty terrifying.

624
01:11:13.985 --> 01:11:18.011
Buddy, you got a dead cat
in there, or what?

625
01:11:25.124 --> 01:11:27.098
Fuck you, asshole.

626
01:11:45.474 --> 01:11:47.132
God damn!

627
01:11:47.202 --> 01:11:49.536
Thank you.

628
01:11:54.497 --> 01:11:56.155
Is this enough?

629
01:11:56.194 --> 01:11:57.600
Yeah, it's enough.

630
01:11:57.633 --> 01:12:00.417
I don't want to ask
where you got it.

631
01:12:05.571 --> 01:12:07.359
- I'm coming.
- We need a room.

632
01:12:07.395 --> 01:12:09.370
- All right.
- With a kitchen.

633
01:12:09.411 --> 01:12:10.939
Do you have one
with a kitchen?

634
01:12:25.890 --> 01:12:28.279
I am dying for a shower.

635
01:12:30.210 --> 01:12:32.577
We should check
your bandage, too.

636
01:12:32.610 --> 01:12:35.610
Later. I'm going out
for supplies.

637
01:12:39.809 --> 01:12:41.565
Keep this.

638
01:13:06.528 --> 01:13:08.220
No, I can't tell you
where I am, Mom.

639
01:13:08.256 --> 01:13:10.146
I was told not to say.

640
01:13:10.179 --> 01:13:11.771
Honey, I need to know
where I can reach you.

641
01:13:11.811 --> 01:13:14.396
You tell me to hide up at
the cabin like some fugitive...

642
01:13:14.434 --> 01:13:17.249
and you won't tell me
what's going on?

643
01:13:17.282 --> 01:13:19.105
I am worried sick, dear.

644
01:13:22.530 --> 01:13:23.437
Here's the number. Ready?

645
01:13:23.471 --> 01:13:24.346
Here's the number. Ready?

646
01:13:24.385 --> 01:13:26.272
Yes. Go ahead.

647
01:13:26.305 --> 01:13:31.061
It's 408-555-1439.

648
01:13:31.104 --> 01:13:32.991
Room nine. Got it?

649
01:13:33.024 --> 01:13:34.202
I've got it.

650
01:13:34.240 --> 01:13:35.483
I've got to go.

651
01:13:35.520 --> 01:13:38.749
I'm sorry I can't
tell you more right now.

652
01:13:38.783 --> 01:13:40.212
I love you, Mom.

653
01:13:43.583 --> 01:13:45.975
I love you, too, sweetheart.

654
01:13:57.602 --> 01:14:00.219
- Tiki Motel.
- Give me your address.

655
01:14:03.265 --> 01:14:04.694
What have we got?

656
01:14:07.584 --> 01:14:09.494
Mothballs.

657
01:14:10.785 --> 01:14:12.824
Corn syrup.

658
01:14:12.864 --> 01:14:14.271
Ammonia.

659
01:14:14.304 --> 01:14:16.191
What's for dinner?

660
01:14:16.224 --> 01:14:17.631
Plastique.

661
01:14:17.664 --> 01:14:19.551
That sounds good.

662
01:14:19.583 --> 01:14:20.928
What is it?

663
01:14:20.961 --> 01:14:22.849
Nitroglycerin, basically.

664
01:14:22.881 --> 01:14:24.769
It's a bit more stable.

665
01:14:24.801 --> 01:14:27.223
I learned to make it
when I was a kid.

666
01:14:38.530 --> 01:14:41.563
Make sure there's none
on the threads.

667
01:14:41.601 --> 01:14:43.674
Like this.

668
01:14:45.920 --> 01:14:47.612
Screw the end cap on.

669
01:14:49.345 --> 01:14:50.719
Very gently.

670
01:14:53.473 --> 01:14:55.894
You must have had
a fun childhood.

671
01:14:58.849 --> 01:15:01.216
That's good.

672
01:15:01.248 --> 01:15:02.906
All right.
Six more like that...

673
01:15:02.944 --> 01:15:04.832
and I'll get started
on the fuses.

674
01:15:15.838 --> 01:15:17.115
He'll find us, won't he?

675
01:15:19.934 --> 01:15:21.364
Probably.

676
01:15:38.720 --> 01:15:40.575
It'll never be over, will it?

677
01:15:49.217 --> 01:15:52.063
Look at me. I'm shaking.

678
01:15:52.096 --> 01:15:54.943
Some legend, huh?

679
01:15:54.975 --> 01:15:58.292
You must be
pretty disappointed.

680
01:15:58.335 --> 01:16:01.684
No. I'm not.

681
01:16:12.737 --> 01:16:15.038
The women in your time...

682
01:16:15.073 --> 01:16:16.982
what are they like?

683
01:16:19.393 --> 01:16:21.280
Good fighters.

684
01:16:21.313 --> 01:16:23.222
That's not what I meant.

685
01:16:25.664 --> 01:16:27.703
Was there someone special?

686
01:16:29.280 --> 01:16:31.516
Someone?

687
01:16:31.552 --> 01:16:33.308
A girl. You know.

688
01:16:39.071 --> 01:16:40.499
Never.

689
01:16:41.950 --> 01:16:43.382
Never?

690
01:16:48.449 --> 01:16:49.976
I'm sorry.

691
01:16:50.017 --> 01:16:51.926
I'm so sorry.

692
01:16:54.306 --> 01:16:57.340
So much pain.

693
01:16:57.378 --> 01:16:59.963
Pain can be controlled.

694
01:17:00.001 --> 01:17:02.106
You just disconnect it.

695
01:17:02.145 --> 01:17:04.086
So you feel nothing?

696
01:17:09.216 --> 01:17:11.736
John Connor gave me
a picture of you once.

697
01:17:13.856 --> 01:17:15.645
I didn't know why at the time.

698
01:17:15.679 --> 01:17:17.949
It was very old...

699
01:17:19.392 --> 01:17:21.431
torn...

700
01:17:21.472 --> 01:17:22.901
faded.

701
01:17:25.951 --> 01:17:28.122
You were young like you are now.

702
01:17:28.159 --> 01:17:32.566
You seemed just a little sad.

703
01:17:32.606 --> 01:17:37.340
I always wondered what you
were thinking at that moment.

704
01:17:37.374 --> 01:17:41.083
I memorized every line...

705
01:17:41.118 --> 01:17:42.974
every curve.

706
01:17:46.302 --> 01:17:48.374
I came across time
for you, Sarah.

707
01:17:49.854 --> 01:17:51.283
I love you.

708
01:17:52.766 --> 01:17:54.292
I always have.

709
01:18:11.296 --> 01:18:13.205
I shouldn't have said that.

710
01:19:40.032 --> 01:19:41.624
Think fast!

711
01:21:07.583 --> 01:21:09.175
Trade places!

712
01:21:19.774 --> 01:21:23.286
Faster! Drive faster!

713
01:22:12.062 --> 01:22:13.916
Oh, my God!

714
01:23:02.077 --> 01:23:03.451
- Whoa!
- Son of a bitch!

715
01:23:18.430 --> 01:23:20.088
You stay here.

716
01:23:42.876 --> 01:23:44.086
Let's get out of here.

717
01:23:47.452 --> 01:23:48.979
Get out.

718
01:24:05.183 --> 01:24:08.030
Kyle! Come on! Get up!

719
01:24:14.270 --> 01:24:17.335
He's coming! Kyle!

720
01:24:17.374 --> 01:24:18.716
Come on!

721
01:24:19.742 --> 01:24:22.524
Help me! Get out!

722
01:24:23.934 --> 01:24:25.078
Get out!

723
01:24:33.565 --> 01:24:34.644
Come on!

724
01:24:40.604 --> 01:24:42.098
Faster!

725
01:24:45.852 --> 01:24:48.120
Don't stop! Run!

726
01:27:07.739 --> 01:27:09.681
We did it, Kyle.

727
01:27:09.723 --> 01:27:11.151
We got it.

728
01:28:26.042 --> 01:28:27.668
Wait!

729
01:28:32.026 --> 01:28:34.392
What are you doing?

730
01:28:34.426 --> 01:28:36.730
Cover... so he can't track us.

731
01:28:46.716 --> 01:28:50.100
Come on!

732
01:28:50.141 --> 01:28:51.547
No, Kyle!

733
01:28:52.636 --> 01:28:54.196
Come on!

734
01:28:54.236 --> 01:28:55.861
Leave me here.

735
01:28:55.900 --> 01:28:57.274
Get up!

736
01:29:06.459 --> 01:29:08.401
Move it, Reese!

737
01:29:08.443 --> 01:29:11.061
On your feet, soldier!

738
01:29:11.098 --> 01:29:14.481
On your feet! Move it!

739
01:30:23.516 --> 01:30:25.425
Back. Go back.

740
01:30:58.364 --> 01:31:00.469
Run, Sarah.

741
01:31:00.508 --> 01:31:02.133
Run!

742
01:31:07.291 --> 01:31:08.753
Come on, motherfucker.

743
01:34:52.216 --> 01:34:54.453
You're terminated, fucker.

744
01:36:11.128 --> 01:36:13.430
Tape 7, November 10.

745
01:36:13.465 --> 01:36:15.025
Where was I?

746
01:36:16.185 --> 01:36:18.192
What's most difficult for me
is trying to decide...

747
01:36:18.233 --> 01:36:20.055
what to tell you
and what not to.

748
01:36:20.089 --> 01:36:21.876
But I guess
I have a while yet...

749
01:36:21.912 --> 01:36:24.694
before you're old enough
to even understand these tapes.

750
01:36:24.728 --> 01:36:26.353
They're more for me
at this point...

751
01:36:26.392 --> 01:36:29.588
just so that
I can get it straight.

752
01:37:04.089 --> 01:37:05.299
Fill her up.

753
01:37:08.696 --> 01:37:11.827
Should I tell you
about your father?

754
01:37:11.863 --> 01:37:13.936
Boy, that's a tough one.

755
01:37:15.385 --> 01:37:17.806
Will it affect your decision
to send him here...

756
01:37:17.848 --> 01:37:20.629
knowing that he is your father?

757
01:37:20.663 --> 01:37:24.438
If you don't send Kyle,
you can never be.

758
01:37:24.471 --> 01:37:27.853
God, a person could go crazy
thinking about this.

759
01:37:31.257 --> 01:37:34.072
I suppose I will tell you.

760
01:37:34.105 --> 01:37:36.494
I owe him that.

761
01:37:38.426 --> 01:37:41.272
Maybe it'll help if...

762
01:37:41.306 --> 01:37:45.942
you know that in the few hours
that we had together...

763
01:37:48.024 --> 01:37:50.708
we loved a lifetime's worth.

764
01:38:02.424 --> 01:38:04.314
What did he just say?

765
01:38:04.347 --> 01:38:06.233
He says
you're very beautiful...

766
01:38:06.266 --> 01:38:07.607
and he's ashamed to ask you...

767
01:38:07.641 --> 01:38:09.463
for five American dollars
for his picture...

768
01:38:09.498 --> 01:38:12.945
but if he doesn't,
his father will beat him.

769
01:38:12.985 --> 01:38:14.545
Pretty good hustle, kid.

770
01:38:30.936 --> 01:38:32.759
What did he just say?

771
01:38:32.793 --> 01:38:35.476
He said
there's a storm coming in.

772
01:38:39.800 --> 01:38:41.229
I know.
